<spell-notebook "description usage">
	<header level="1">
		Description
		<header>A description is the text of a card, item, modal, list item, step or comment.</>
	</>
	<description-tab-bar showing="usage"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#using-it">Using it</>
			<item link="#owners">Owners</>
			<item link="#accessibility">Accessibility</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Using it">
		<markdown>
			`<ui-description>` describes its owner's content: a card's or an item's text, a comment's text (Fomantic's comment
			`text`), a list item's or a step's second line, a modal's text beside an image.

			- No attributes: the owner decides the look (a card's muted text, a comment's body, a step's smaller line).
			- Put paragraphs, links or other parts inside it.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Owners">
		<markdown>
			`<ui-description>` finds its nearest owner and sets `:state(in-<owner>)` on itself; `UIParts.css` styles it by that
			state. Its owners, and what each makes of it:

			- [Card](/components/ui/ui-card.html) (`:state(in-card)`): muted body text under the header and meta
			- [Item](/components/ui/ui-items.html) (`:state(in-item)`): body text, with space above
			- [Comment](/components/ui/ui-comment.html) (`:state(in-comment)`): the comment's text
			- [Modal](/components/ui/ui-modal.html) (`:state(in-modal)`): the text beside an `image` content's image
			- [Flyout](/components/ui/ui-flyout.html) (`:state(in-flyout)`): body text
			- [List](/components/ui/ui-list.html) (`:state(in-list)`): a second, muted line under the item's header
			- [Step](/components/ui/ui-step.html) (`:state(in-step)`): a smaller line under the step's title
			- [Search](/components/ui/ui-search.html) (`:state(in-search)`): a search result's second line

			Anywhere else it is an unstyled block. More on how parts find their owners: [Content parts](/components/ui/ui-header.html).
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Accessibility">
		<markdown>
			- A neutral block with no role. Use real elements inside it (`<p>`, `<a>`, lists) for structure.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
